# THE HOLDING'S DAILY COPY — systemd USER unit (install: scripts/systemd/install.sh).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS, and it is a repair, not a new idea. The company's database was
# dumped nightly and shipped to the Hetzner Storage Box from 2026-07-18. The
# move to the workstation (board row B29) carried the repository, the database,
# the keys and the toolchain — and left the SCHEDULE behind on the X230: the
# script's own header still installs a cron line under /home/ghost. Measured
# 2026-08-27: no crontab for this user, no dxb timer of any kind, and the last
# automatic dump was 2026-08-13. Thirteen days in which the holding existed on
# one desk and nowhere else.
#
# It writes a custom-format pg_dump of the COMPANY engine
# (supabase_db_DxB_Global_OS) to ~/backups/dxb, copies it to the Storage Box
# over the `dxb-storagebox` SSH host block, and prunes local copies older than
# 14 days. It opens no other door and carries no credential of its own.
[Unit]
Description=DXB — daily dump of the holding's database, with the off-site copy

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/bash "%h/DxB Global OS/scripts/backup/laptop-pg-dump.sh"
StandardOutput=append:%h/backups/dxb/backup.log
StandardError=append:%h/backups/dxb/backup.log
